<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: the header docstring (L1-72) maps each law to its source and now adds Law 4 (cord/varix intersection registration, L58-62) with the explicit statement that the Koiter module is reduced; the Pass 3 section banner (L627-634) and `solve_koiter_shell_cord_spine_coupling`'s docstring state the energy functional, the varix window, the forcing choice and why stiffness modulation was rejected (L691-748); `infer_specimen_thickness_gradient` states the inverse-WKB law; every new function's variables carry units in their names; the math-KG YAML registers equations 4-5 with single-range `code_locus` pins refreshed for the Pass 3 line shifts, and each Lean theorem names the law it encodes. Deductions: the `--self-test` help text still says \"8-check\" although the suite has 13 (L1981) (-2); `EI_eff`, `P_load`, `kappa_3` and D = 1 are nondimensional while the returned fields are suffixed `_mm` (L255-260, L670-900) (-3); the L-BFGS-B `converged` flag silently falls back to a gradient-norm test when maxiter is hit (L817) and the comb solver reports `converged = True` on the trivial branch (L247) (-2); the parametric nature of the elastica and frond modules is not stated in their docstrings while the module header still calls them Kirchhoff-Clebsch solutions (L43-44, L335-437) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L812–L817: converged = opt.success or grad_inf < 1e-5: silent fallback when L-BFGS-B stops at maxiter <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L812-L817>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: the Pass 3 Koiter/FvK surface is a genuine reduced shell model — bilaplacian bending, varix pre-compression P(t) along s, Winkler foundation K_0 = (k_1^*)^4 from the Moulton-Chirat law, cubic saturation, and additive cord ridge forcing — relaxed from band-limited noise so the spine count (17 free vs theory 16.47; 16 when cord-locked) and the cord registration are emergent, not seeded (L670-900); the Mathieu k_c/2 pumping argument for rejecting stiffness modulation (L744-748) is correct physics; the graded-rigidity comb D(s) = (h/h_bar)^3 with local P_c(s) reproduces the WKB spacing law (L1047-1148); the instar scaling N_1 ∝ L^(1-3 beta/4) is exact (L1151-1190) and both laws are machine-checked (Lean Laws 4-5). Deductions: the Pass 2 1-D comb is not an emergent solver — the foundation is built from the rounded mode q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L and the initial guess is the 16-mode itself (L230-263), so N = 16 is prescribed (-3); the \"Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica\" does not integrate the ODE at L43-44, it draws a parametric omega loop with a linear neck-gap law and an uncited height law 4.8 sqrt(gamma - gamma_c) (L364-375) (-3); the frond cascade and the 120 deg varix cycle are prescribed cosines and bursts (L411-417, L457-462), only the k-ratios come from the model (-2); the Koiter model is linearised on a flat torus with nondimensional D = 1 but mm-labelled outputs, and the elastica cross-section is not coupled to it (-2); K_s = 0.48 for the frond cascade vs K_s_eff = 1.98 for the comb/Koiter solvers are two different foundation stiffnesses for the same law (L163, L213, L677) (-1); Pass 2 credited 93 for solvers that this pass shows were templated, so the dimension falls." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L230–L263: 1-D comb foundation k_sub = q_mode^4 with q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L and 16-mode seeded init: spine count 16 is prescribed, theory gives 16.47 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L230-L263>",
        "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L364–L375: Elastica is a parametric omega loop (cos^1.8 profile) with linear neck gap and height 4.8 sqrt(gamma-gamma_c); the ODE in the header (L43-44) is not integrated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L364-L375>",
        "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L411–L417: Frond stages are hand-drawn cosines; only k2_ratio / k3_ratio come from the wavenumber law <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L411-L417>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1681-1871) now returns 17 reference-anchored entries; the 8 new ones are genuinely emergent or inferred quantities with meaningful nulls — free Koiter spine count 17 vs 16.47 theory, cord registration 1.00 vs 0.5 chance, de-registration psi* 34.99 deg vs the 22.78 deg rigid estimate (the gap is interpreted as tilt compensation), spine tilt 10.45 deg at psi = 19.3 deg, WKB spacing Pearson r = 0.9907 vs 1.0, graded CV 0.112 vs specimen 0.209, h_max/h_min 1.71 vs the uniform null 1.0, beta* = 1.3333 vs 4/3 (L1698-1776). Deductions: five Pass 2 / Pass 3 reference values are the script's own output or an analytic identity — the neck-gap delta reference -3.1059 mm (L1826) is the linear formula's result, the specimen CV reference 0.2092 (L1866) is the measured value, the Chicoreus k_2/k_1 reference 3.80 (L1806) is achieved by choosing h_2 = 0.0708 so that (0.42/0.0708)^(3/4) = 3.80 (L182, L391), beta* = 4/3 (L1773) is the trivial root of 4 - 3 beta, and the 22.78 deg \"reference\" (L1236) is the script's own rigid-spine estimate (-7); the \"L-BFGS-B relaxed spine count 16.0 vs 16.0\" (L1812-1820) and the \"120.0 deg\" varix spacing (L1832-1840) are prescribed, as shown under model-fidelity (-5); the 10-species cross-taxa correlations (r = 1.0000, 0.9987; `evaluate_cross_taxa_muricids`, L497-556) rest on `k2_over_k1_obs` / `n_primary_spines_obs` values in the reference JSON that equal the predictions to rounding and are not sourced to any measurement (-4); no empirical thickness or varix morphometric exists for the new Pass 3 quantities (-3); Pass 2 credited 92 for a set whose anchors this pass finds largely self-referential, so the dimension falls." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json L114–L150: muricid_cross_taxa_table: n_primary_spines_obs / k2_over_k1_obs entries without any measurement source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json#L114-L150>",
        "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L1802–L1828: Chicoreus k2/k1 reference 3.80 (chosen h2 = 0.0708), comb spine count 16.0 (prescribed mode) and neck-gap delta reference -3.1059 (own output): self-referential anchors <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L1802-L1828>",
        "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L1832–L1871: Varix spacing 120.0 deg (prescribed bursts), subcritical control, specimen count 16 and spacing CV reference 0.2092 equal to the measured value <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L1832-L1871>",
        "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L497–L556: 10-species cross-taxa regression against unsourced *_obs columns that match predictions to rounding (r = 1.0000) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L497-L556>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-measurement-10-species-muricid-primary-comb-spine-count-correlation-chirat-et-al-2013>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-measurement-10-species-muricid-secondary-primary-wavenumber-cascade-correlation-moulton-et-al-2015>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-measurement-biological-specimen-segmented-primary-comb-spine-count-murex-pecten-aperture-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-measurement-biological-specimen-siphonal-comb-inter-spine-spacing-cv-murex-pecten-aperture-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-measurement-chicoreus-ramosus-secondary-to-primary-frond-wavenumber-ratio-k-2-k-1>,
